  "title": "Disaster recovery and backup across two sites and a cloud tier",
  "description": "The primary datacenter runs the application behind an HA firewall pair with a PostgreSQL primary; Veeam backs it up to a storage array that copies to tape and replicates to the DR site; the database streams to a hot standby in DC2 over the site-to-site link, and monthly tape copies land in S3 Glacier Deep Archive as the off-site tier.",
